        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "When the captureMetaData option is enabled, every parsed element node carries a metadata object (under the symbol returned by XMLParser.getMetaDataSymbol()) that currently holds only startIndex, the offset of the node's opening \"<\". Add endIndex to that same metadata object: the exclusive offset just past the last character of the node in the input string, so that input.slice(startIndex, endIndex) is the node's full source text. It must be set for paired elements (the position after the closing tag's \">\"), self-closing elements (after \"/>\"), unpaired tags configured through unpairedTags, and processing-instruction nodes (after \"?>\"); nested elements each get their own value; it must work in both the default and the preserveOrder output, and the updateTag option must not disturb a sibling's indices. Declare the field in the TypeScript types in src/fxp.d.ts. Source is under src/; tests run with npm test (jasmine).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
